🎯 One answer that covers almost everything

If the interviewer asks “How do you handle dropdowns in Selenium?”, give this:

“First I identify the type of dropdown. If it is a standard HTML <select> element, I use Selenium's Select class and methods such as selectByVisibleText, selectByValue, or selectByIndex. If it is a custom dropdown, I click the dropdown, locate the available options and select the required option based on visible text or a stable attribute. For dynamic or auto-suggest dropdowns, I enter the required text, use an explicit wait for the suggestions to appear, iterate through the suggestions, and click the matching option. I avoid hardcoded indexes when the option order can change.”
